    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26999" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δί-κροτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>double-beating,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥόθια κώπας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					408
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); of the pulse, <i><span class="en">
				Archig.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.537
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Syn.Puls.</u>
				8.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of ships,
				<i>with only two banks of oars manned,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.1.28
			</span></i>; later, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διήρης</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.5.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Am.</u>
				6
			</span></i>: Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκροτον, τό,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.62.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Mith.</u>
				17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκροτος, ἡ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.640
			</span></i> (Antip.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἁμαξιτός</span> a road <i>for two
				carriages,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				775
			</span></i>.</div>
